= Reproducibility — Simple =

'''Reproducibility''' means being able to repeat a result under clearly specified conditions.

In computational science, a common modern meaning is:

<blockquote>Use the same data and the same analysis, and get a consistent computational result.</blockquote>

To do that, another researcher may need:

* the data;
* the exact code;
* software versions;
* settings;
* processing steps;
* the computing environment.

[[Version control/Simple|Version control]] and [[Provenance/Simple|provenance]] can help record this information.

Reproducibility is not the same as [[Replication/Simple|replication]].

Replication usually means doing a new study or collecting new data to ask the same scientific question.

A result can also be perfectly reproducible and still be wrong if the same mistake is repeated every time.

